ok§chapter «first_verseªlast_verse¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+And when the LORD saw it, he abhorred them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ;Because of the provoking of his sons, and of his daughters.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ+And he said, I will hide my face from them,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#I will see what their end shall be:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ'For they are a very froward generation,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text½Children in whom is no faith.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ:They have moved me to jealousy with that which is not God;¦layout ‚¤textÙ3They have provoked me to anger with their vanities:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙCAnd I will move them to jealousy with those which are not a people;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ3I will provoke them to anger with a foolish nation.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ$For a fire is kindled in mine anger,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And shall burn unto the lowest hell,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ.And shall consume the earth with her increase,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ1And set on fire the foundations of the mountains.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ I will heap mischiefs upon them;¦layout ‚¤textÙ#I will spend mine arrows upon them.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ@They shall be burnt with hunger, and devoured with burning heat,¦layout ‚¤text¼And with bitter destruction:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ/I will also send the teeth of beasts upon them,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ(With the poison of serpents of the dust.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤text²The sword without,¦layout ‚¤text²And terror within,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ0Shall destroy both the young man and the virgin,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ-The suckling also with the man of gray hairs.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ*I said, I would scatter them into corners,¦layout ‚¤textÙ=I would make the remembrance of t