yout§quote_1ªlast_verse#…¤book§chapter «first_verse$ªlast_verse+¦verses˜„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines”‚¤textÙ$For the LORD shall judge his people,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And repent himself for his servants,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ'When he seeth that their power is gone,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ#And there is none shut up, or left.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'And he shall say, Where are their gods,¦layout ‚¤textÙ Their rock in whom they trusted,¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ*Which did eat the fat of their sacrifices,¦layout ‚¤textÙ,And drank the wine of their drink offerings?¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¾Let them rise up and help you,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text·And be your protection.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines•‚¤text¾See now that I, even I, am he,¦layout ‚¤text¼And there is no god with me:¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¹I kill, and I make alive;¦layout§quote_1‚¤text´I wound, and I heal:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ5Neither is there any that can deliver out of my hand.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ For I lift up my hand to heaven,¦layout ‚¤text¹And say, I live for ever.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤text¾If I whet my glittering sword,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$And mine hand take hold on judgment;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ(I will render vengeance to mine enemies,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ"And will reward them that hate me.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ)I will make mine arrows drunk with blood,¦layout ‚¤textÙ And my sword shall devour flesh;¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ9And that with the blood of the slain and of the captives,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ.From the beginning of revenges upon the enemy.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ'Rejoice, O ye nations, with his people:¦layout ‚¤textÙ-For he will avenge the blood of his servants,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ-And will render vengeance to his adversaries,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ6And will be merciful unto his land, and to his people.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse+…¤book§chapter «first_verse,ªlast_verse/¦verses”„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmAnd Moses came and spake all the words of this song in the ears of the people, he, and Hoshea the son of Nun.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@And Moses made an end of speaking all these words to all Israel:¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯and he said unto them, Set your hearts unto all the words which I testify among you this day, which ye shall command your children to observe to do, all the words of this law.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤For it is not a vain thing for you; because it is your life: and through this thing ye shall prolong your days in the land, whither ye go over Jordan to possess it.¦layout ªlast_verse/…¤book§chapter «first_verse0ªlast_verse4¦verses•„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8And the LORD spake unto Moses that selfsame day, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍGet thee up into this mountain Abarim, unto mount Nebo, which is in the land of Moab, that is over against Jericho; and behold the land of Canaan, which I give unto the children of Israel for a possession:¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–and die in the mount whither thou goest up, and be gathered unto thy people; as Aaron thy brother died in mount Hor, and was gathered unto his people:¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ½because ye trespassed against me among the children of Israel at the waters of Meribah-Kadesh, in the wilderness of Zin; because ye sanctified me not in the midst of the children of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyYet thou shalt see the land before thee; but thou shalt not go thither unto the land which I give the children of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse4